Design spec:
{"id":"REQ-REQUIREMENT","revision":1,"rawText":"Add a GET /api/v1/urls/{code}/preview endpoint that fetches the HTML page pointed to by the short code's target URL, extracts the page title and meta description, caches the result, and returns it to the caller so they can preview a link before following it. If the short code is unknown the endpoint returns 404. External fetching must be time-bounded to avoid hanging the request.","normalizedProblem":"Add a GET /api/v1/urls/{code}/preview endpoint that fetches the HTML page pointed to by the short code's target URL, extracts the page title and meta description, caches the result, and returns it to the caller so they can preview a link before following it. If the short code is unknown the endpoint returns 404. External fetching must be time-bounded to avoid hanging the request.","acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"AC-1","description":"GET /api/v1/urls/{code}/preview returns HTTP 200 with a JSON body containing at least a 'title' field and a 'description' field when the short code exists and the target page is reachable.","riskLevel":"HIGH"},{"id":"AC-2","description":"The 'title' field in the response is populated from the target page's <title> element.","riskLevel":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"AC-3","description":"The 'description' field in the response is populated from the target page's <meta name='description'> content attribute.","riskLevel":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"AC-4","description":"When the short code does not exist in the system, the endpoint returns HTTP 404, consistent with the existing lookup and redirect endpoints.","riskLevel":"HIGH"},{"id":"AC-5","description":"Preview data for a given short code is cached after the first successful (or partially successful) fetch, so that subsequent requests for the same code do not trigger a new external HTTP request.","riskLevel":"HIGH"},{"id":"AC-6","description":"A timeout is applied to the outbound HTTP request to the target URL. If the target does not respond within the timeout, the endpoint returns a response (HTTP 200 or a defined partial-result status) with empty or null values for 'title' and/or 'description' rather than blocking indefinitely.","riskLevel":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"AC-7","description":"If the target URL is unreachable (DNS failure, connection refused, etc.), the endpoint returns a sensible partial or empty result rather than a 5xx error, analogous to the timeout behavior.","riskLevel":"HIGH"},{"id":"AC-8","description":"The endpoint follows the same {code} path-parameter convention as the existing lookup and redirect endpoints.","riskLevel":"LOW"},{"id":"AC-9","description":"The outbound fetch request identifies itself with a recognizable User-Agent so target servers can identify and manage the scraper traffic.","riskLevel":"MEDIUM"}],"ambiguities":["The requirement says 'return a sensible partial or empty result' on timeout or unreachability, but does not specify the HTTP status code for that response (200 with nulls, 206, 422, 503, etc.).","It is unclear whether the cache should be invalidated or refreshed, and if so under what conditions (TTL expiry, manual purge, short-code deletion, target URL update).","The requirement does not define what 'cached' means in terms of storage — in-memory, Redis, database, CDN, etc.","It is unspecified whether the endpoint should follow HTTP redirects when fetching the target URL (some long URLs may themselves redirect).","The requirement does not clarify how to handle target pages that return non-HTML content types (PDFs, images, JSON APIs). It is unclear whether to attempt extraction, return empty fields, or return an error.","It is ambiguous whether both 'title' and 'description' must always be present in the response body (possibly null/empty) or whether absent fields may be omitted entirely.","The requirement does not specify the exact timeout value, nor whether it should be configurable.","It is unclear whether the response should include the resolved target URL itself alongside the preview metadata."],"assumptions":["The HTTP response status for a timed-out or unreachable fetch will be 200 with null/empty 'title' and 'description' fields, so clients receive a consistent schema and can distinguish the partial result from a code-not-found (404).","Cache entries will have a time-to-live (TTL) after which the next request triggers a fresh external fetch; the TTL value will be defined during implementation and should be configurable.","The endpoint will follow a reasonable number of HTTP redirects (e.g., up to 5) when fetching the target URL.","Non-HTML responses will yield null/empty 'title' and 'description' without causing the endpoint to return an error status.","Both 'title' and 'description' fields will always be present in the response body, using null when the value cannot be determined.","The timeout value will be configurable via service configuration rather than hard-coded, with a sensible default (e.g., 5 seconds) chosen during implementation.","The preview fetch is performed lazily on first request rather than eagerly at short-code creation time.","Failed fetches (timeout, unreachable) will also be cached for a shorter negative-cache TTL to prevent repeated hammering of a broken target."],"outOfScope":["Open Graph (og:title, og:description, og:image) or Twitter Card metadata extraction — only <title> and <meta name='description'> are in scope.","Thumbnail or screenshot generation for the target URL.","Any preview mechanism triggered at short-code creation time (eager/background prefetch).","Modifying, creating, or deleting short codes via this endpoint.","Authentication or authorization for accessing the preview endpoint (not mentioned in the requirement).","Any existing preview mechanism (the requirement explicitly states none exists)."]}
